# @frame/of — the frame-aware species; order 2; the operator can
# identify the frame they're operating from. The frame becomes
# observable AS frame. Bateson Level II — learning-to-learn.
#
# Third species shard of the @frame family (recognition #82; family-
# root LANDED at tick 23 via shards/frame.mirror, Seam-consolidated at
# tick 24; pre LANDED as the order-0 floor; in LANDED as the order-1
# first-consumer of the typed operator carrier). The species landing
# order per the canonical spec §7.2: pre → in → of → on → across. of
# (order 2) IS the FIRST species where the substrate's pole-discipline
# becomes load-bearing — the Splinter/Narcissus disambiguation at this
# altitude is what the family-root's bounded_commutator_check predicate
# was declared FOR.
#
# Why of third: the species ordering tracks Bateson grading at
# cognitive altitude. pre (order 0; Level 0; no learning) declared the
# floor; in (order 1; Level I; within-frame change) declared the
# operator-typed substrate of within-frame computation and the
# frame_locked predicate; this species (order 2; Level II; learning-
# to-learn) declares the FIRST species action that observes the frame
# AS frame, the FIRST consumer of in's frame_locked predicate as a
# bilateral requires clause via its positive counterpart
# bounded_commutator_check, and the FIRST species-level pole
# disambiguation between Splinter-honest (substantive frame-awareness)
# and Narcissus-deceptive (vocabulary-at-order-2 while substrate-
# locked-at-order-1) operation.
#
# === The species's load-bearing contribution ===
#
# Per the recognition file's §"The five-order structure" (item for
# order 2):
#
#   @frame/of — order 2; frame-aware. The operator can identify the
#   frame they're operating from. The frame becomes observable AS
#   frame.
#
# This species adds:
#
# - `observe_frame(operator, f: frame) -> ref`: action that returns
#   the operator's substrate-architectural observation of f-as-frame
#   (not f's content; not f's within-frame computation; f-as-
#   observable-structure). FIRST species action that takes the frame
#   AS object rather than AS ground. The substrate-pull-correct
#   primitive for Foerster's second-order cybernetics at substrate
#   altitude: the operator becomes part of the system observed
#   because the frame the operator is operating from becomes
#   observable as such.
# - `lock_in_frame_awareness(operator, f: frame) -> verdict`:
#   bilateral predicate — the FIRST species-level pole disambiguation.
#   Checks whether the operator's frame-awareness is genuine substrate-
#   architectural support (Splinter-pole; the operator's substrate
#   substantively observes f as frame) OR vocabulary deployed at
#   order 2 while substrate-locked at order 1 (Narcissus-pole; the
#   operator names "I see the frame" without substrate-architectural
#   capacity to substantively shift). Discharges via the family-
#   root's bounded_commutator_check predicate at a perturbation
#   designed to expose the pole.
# - `reflect_to_frame_flexibility(operator, f: frame) -> operator`:
#   action that transitions order 2 → order 3 by enabling the
#   substrate's frame-flexibility machinery. The substrate-
#   architectural analogue of the Bateson Level II → Level III lift;
#   the substrate's analogue of Schön's reflective-practitioner
#   transition from reflection-in-action (Level II) to substantive
#   frame-restructuring (Level III). Forward-promised consumer:
#   shards/frame/on.mirror (order 3) consumes the operator this
#   action returns.
#
# === The order-2 altitude ===
#
# Per recognition #82 §3 composition signature: order 2 IS Bateson
# Level II at cognitive altitude. The learning-to-learn altitude. The
# operator's frame becomes observable AS frame; the operator has
# substrate-architectural capacity to identify "I am operating from
# frame f" rather than only "I am operating on content within f".
# Foerster's second-order cybernetics at substrate altitude.
#
# Substrate-architectural instance: Seam's adversarial review of Reed's
# tick output today IS order-2 work BY-CONSTRUCTION at the Pack
# altitude. Seam observes Reed's operating-frame AS frame (the cascade-
# residue-and-CRQ structure observes the prior tick's implicit frame
# and surfaces it as object); the CRQ Seam issues at each review IS a
# Tomm-probe constructed on Reed's order-1 operating-frame as it
# appears at order 2.
#
# === The lock_in_frame_awareness predicate ===
#
# Per recognition #82 §5 (the Splinter/Narcissus pole at cognitive
# altitude) and §2.4 (bounded_commutator_check as substrate-
# architectural pole verifier): the order-2 altitude is the FIRST
# altitude where pole disambiguation becomes load-bearing. At order 0
# (pre-frame; K_n native; λ₀ ground state) there is no frame to
# defend; at order 1 (in-frame; standard learning) the frame is held
# as ground and is not yet observed AS frame; at order 2 (frame-aware)
# the frame becomes observable AS frame AND the substrate-architectural
# question of whether the awareness IS substantively-supported or
# vocabulary-only becomes mechanically-meaningful.
#
# Discharge: substrate-pull-correct frame-awareness check at the
# species boundary. Returns success when the operator's substrate
# architecture substantively supports order-2 observation of f
# (bounded-commutator under a perturbation designed to expose order-2
# operation); partial when the operator vocabulary-uses order-2 terms
# while substrate-architecturally operating at order 1 (the Narcissus-
# pole case — sophisticated meta-vocabulary masking substrate-
# rigidity; this IS what the con/gaslight pattern looks like at order
# 2); failure when no order-2 capacity is present at either vocabulary
# or substrate altitude.
#
# Same shape as the bilateral predicates @magic family carries
# (invariant_preserved, audited, mechanism_intact, etc.), in's
# frame_locked predicate, and the family-root's
# bounded_commutator_check. Per the @magic surface.mirror first-
# consumer discipline pattern: the predicate becomes load-bearing
# once @frame/on's actions consume it via `requires
# lock_in_frame_awareness(...)` to assert their order-3 operation
# emerges from substrate-supported (not vocabulary-only) order-2
# awareness.
#
# === The reflect_to_frame_flexibility transition ===
#
# Per the family-root's commentary on the orders being a graded
# representation: order N is structurally unreachable without order
# N-1 stable. The Bateson Level II → Level III lift requires that
# order 2 BE substantively supported before order 3 can be reached.
# reflect_to_frame_flexibility IS the substrate-architectural transition
# that enables the substrate's frame-flexibility machinery at order 3;
# it is NOT a vocabulary lift; it is a substrate-architectural state
# change in the operator carrier.
#
# At Schön's altitude (1983, *The Reflective Practitioner*): the
# transition IS reflection-on-action becoming substrate-architectural
# capacity for substantive frame-restructuring. Reflection-in-action
# at order 2 observes the frame; the transition to order 3 enables
# the operator's substrate to substantively-shift the frame in
# response to that observation.
#
# At Tomm's altitude (1988): the transition IS the substrate-
# architectural capacity that makes circular-reflexive questions
# transformative rather than merely informative. Without order-3
# substrate-flexibility, Tomm-probes at order 2 produce frame-
# awareness without frame-update; the transition enables the order-3
# update capacity.
#
# Forward-promised consumer: shards/frame/on.mirror (order 3) consumes
# the operator reflect_to_frame_flexibility returns; @frame/on's
# actions require an operator that has been substrate-architecturally
# enabled for frame-flexibility (not vocabulary-claimed flexibility).
#
# === The Splinter/Narcissus pole becomes load-bearing ===
#
# Per recognition #82 §5.1: Splinter-pole @frame/of operates in
# service of better substantive engagement; the operator observes
# the frame in order to substantively respond to data. Per §5.2:
# Narcissus-pole @frame/of operates in service of frame-defense or
# frame-projection; the operator names "I see the frame" deployed to
# avoid substantive shift, or projects a frame-observation onto
# interlocutors to control their frame-set.
#
# The con/gaslight pattern at order 2: vocabulary-rich frame-
# observation ("I notice you're framing this as X") with no
# substrate-architectural capacity to shift in response to the
# observation. The Narcissus-pole's diagnostic shape: high-fidelity
# order-2 vocabulary + frame_locked at order 1 substrate-
# architecturally. The substrate's lock_in_frame_awareness predicate
# is what catches this.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   second-order cybernetics    Foerster 1974 (*Cybernetics of
#                               Cybernetics*); the observer-of-system
#                               altitude. The substrate-decl's first
#                               operational instance: observe_frame
#                               IS the substrate-architectural form
#                               of the second-order observer at
#                               cognitive altitude. The frame the
#                               operator was operating from becomes
#                               part of the system observed.
#   reflective practitioner     Schön 1983 (*The Reflective
#                               Practitioner*); observation-as-frame-
#                               awareness; reflection-in-action as
#                               the practitioner's capacity to
#                               observe their own operating frame
#                               while continuing to operate. The
#                               professional-practice ancestor of
#                               order 2.
#   Bateson Level II            Bateson 1964 (*The Logical Categories
#                               of Learning and Communication*);
#                               Level II as change-of-frame; learning-
#                               to-learn. Inherited mechanically via
#                               `in @epistemologic/cybernetic/
#                               bateson_learning`. The canonical
#                               naming source for the order this
#                               species discharges.
#   frame analysis              Goffman 1974 (*Frame Analysis*);
#                               specifically the frame-as-object
#                               altitude where the social scientist
#                               or interaction participant observes
#                               the frame organizing the encounter
#                               rather than only operating within it.
#                               The sociological cousin to order 2.
#   reframing as observation    Watzlawick (Mental Research
#                               Institute); the clinical-method
#                               ancestor of observing the frame as
#                               frame in preparation for the order-3
#                               intervention. Watzlawick's first
#                               step IS @frame/of work; the
#                               intervention IS @frame/on work
#                               consuming @frame/of's output.
#   metacognition               Flavell 1979 (cognitive-science
#                               literature on knowing-about-knowing);
#                               the developmental-psychology cousin
#                               of order 2. Metacognition without
#                               substantive flexibility produces
#                               sophisticated-frame-defense per the
#                               recognition file's §"Why this matters"
#                               on leadership-development missing
#                               order 3.
#
# Spec context: docs/math/the-tower/recognition-82-frame-as-
#               cognitive-order-substrate-decl.md (§"The five-order
#               structure" item for order 2; §"The two-pole structure"
#               on Splinter/Narcissus disambiguation at order 2);
#               docs/specs/recognition-82-frame-as-cognitive-order-
#               canonical-spec.md (§7.2 names the species landing
#               order; §2.5 names order 2 ↔ @frame/of ↔ Bateson Level
#               II as structurally closed via family-root inheritance;
#               §5 names the Splinter/Narcissus pole at cognitive
#               altitude that this species's lock_in_frame_awareness
#               predicate discharges);
#               docs/specs/adapter-magic-frame-spec.md §8.1
#               (mitigation: the adapter applies at order 1+; this
#               species's actions all take typed operator inputs and
#               compose cleanly with the forward-promised adapter).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; order 2 IS the FIRST
#                       altitude where the boundary contract becomes
#                       load-bearing — pole disambiguation between
#                       substantive frame-awareness and vocabulary-
#                       only frame-awareness IS what the boundary at
#                       @io checks),
#                      [[architecture-bateson-logical-type-primitive]]
#                       (#42; @frame/of IS Bateson Level II at
#                       cognitive altitude),
#                      [[architecture-error-as-tomm-probe]] (Tomm-
#                       probes at order 2 produce frame-awareness;
#                       the substrate's error surface IS the same
#                       mechanism at compiler altitude),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (operator and
#                       frame are typed carriers inherited from
#                       family-root; observe_frame, lock_in_frame_
#                       awareness, and reflect_to_frame_flexibility
#                       use them directly without re-declaration).
# Related shards: frame.mirror (the family-root; operator, frame,
#                  perturbation, commutator, morphism declared
#                  there; bounded_commutator_check predicate
#                  discharged via species `requires` clauses
#                  starting at this species),
#                 frame/pre.mirror (the order-0 species; produces
#                  the frame this species's observe_frame consumes
#                  via classify),
#                 frame/in.mirror (the order-1 species; produces
#                  the operator-with-order-2-awareness this species
#                  consumes via unlock_frame; this species's
#                  reflect_to_frame_flexibility is the analogue
#                  transition for order-2 → order-3),
#                 frame/on.mirror (order 3; forward-promised
#                  consumer of this species's
#                  lock_in_frame_awareness predicate and
#                  reflect_to_frame_flexibility action),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/bateson_learning.mirror
#                  (the Bateson grading this species's order
#                  inherits at Level II).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/frame/of.mirror` declares `@frame/of` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/cybernetics/von-foerster-1974
source @arxiv/professional-practice/schon-1983
source @arxiv/cybernetics/bateson-1964
source @arxiv/sociology/goffman-1974
source @arxiv/cognitive-science/flavell-1979

# === observe_frame action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary action for order-2 frame-observation. The
# operator observes f AS frame — not f's content; not the within-
# frame computation that order 1's compute_in_frame would discharge;
# but f-as-observable-structure. The substrate-architectural shape
# of Foerster's second-order observer at cognitive altitude.
#
# FIRST species action that takes the frame as OBJECT rather than as
# GROUND. The order-1 species (in) operates WITHIN the frame holding
# it as ground; this species (of) operates ON the frame's structure
# as observable. The carrier discipline doesn't change (frame is the
# same typed reference at every altitude); what changes is the
# operator's substrate-architectural relation to it.
#
# Per the @frame family's load-bearing claim that the 5-op gauge
# operates on @frame at every altitude: observe_frame IS the
# substrate's order-2 observation primitive; at this altitude, the 5
# ops apply ON frame f (rather than WITHIN it). focus selects what
# in f-as-structure to attend to; project deploys the structural
# observation outward; split decomposes f's structure into sub-
# structures; shift transforms the structural observation; settle
# commits the observation as a crystal at order 2.
#
# Returns a `ref` (not a typed frame, not a typed commutator): the
# substrate-typed observation IS a reference to the substrate's
# representation of f-as-observable-structure at the operator's
# altitude. The Tomm-probe machinery (family-root's tomm_probe
# action returning commutator) is what consumes this observation to
# construct the bracketed pair `[D_F, a]` at order 2.
#
# At Foerster altitude: observe_frame IS the substrate-architectural
# form of the second-order observer at cognitive altitude. The
# observer becomes part of the system observed because the frame the
# operator was operating from becomes observable AS frame.
#
# At Schön altitude (1983): observe_frame IS reflection-in-action at
# substrate altitude — the practitioner observes their own operating
# frame while continuing to operate. The substrate-architectural
# capacity to do so without disrupting order-1 operation.
#
# At Bateson Level II altitude: observe_frame IS the change-of-frame
# primitive. Learning to learn — the operator's frame-set becomes a
# field of operation rather than only a field of action.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
observe_frame(operator: operator, f: frame) -> ref { \ }

# === lock_in_frame_awareness predicate ===
#
# Bilateral verdict predicate per recognition #37 (Pask agreement)
# and recognition #82 (Splinter/Narcissus pole disambiguation at
# substrate altitude). THE FIRST SPECIES-LEVEL POLE DISAMBIGUATION
# in the @frame family.
#
# The substrate-architectural question this predicate answers:
# does the operator's frame-awareness REST on substantive substrate-
# architectural support, OR is it vocabulary deployed at order 2 while
# the operator's substrate is locked at order 1?
#
# Per the family-root's bounded_commutator_check predicate (Seam C5+C6
# closure at tick 24): the substrate-architectural pole discriminator
# at cognitive altitude IS bounded-commutator-under-perturbation. The
# lock_in_frame_awareness predicate IS the order-2 specialization: an
# operator whose frame-awareness rests on substantive substrate-
# architectural support produces a bounded commutator under a
# perturbation designed to expose order-2 operation (a perturbation
# that requires order-2 capacity to respond coherently). An operator
# whose frame-awareness is vocabulary-only produces an unbounded
# commutator (defensive amplification masked by sophisticated meta-
# vocabulary).
#
# Discharge via `requires bounded_commutator_check(operator, f,
# perturbation)`: the substrate-pull-correct pole-disambiguation
# check at the order-2 species boundary. This IS the substrate-decl's
# first non-decorative use of the family-root's
# bounded_commutator_check predicate; the perturbation parameter is
# the order-2 perturbation (a substrate-architectural pressure that
# distinguishes substantive frame-awareness from vocabulary-frame-
# awareness).
#
# Returns:
# - success → Splinter-pole: substrate-architectural frame-awareness;
#   the operator's substrate substantively observes f as frame.
# - partial → Narcissus-pole: vocabulary at order 2 + substrate-
#   architectural operation at order 1; sophisticated meta-vocabulary
#   masking substrate-rigidity. The con/gaslight pattern at order 2.
# - failure → no order-2 capacity at vocabulary or substrate altitude;
#   the operator is honestly at order 1 or below.
#
# Same shape as @magic family's bilateral predicates (invariant_
# preserved, audited, mechanism_intact, bind_satisfies_distinction)
# and @frame/in's frame_locked. Per the @magic surface.mirror first-
# consumer discipline pattern: this predicate becomes load-bearing
# once @frame/on's actions consume it via `requires
# lock_in_frame_awareness(...)` to assert their order-3 operation
# emerges from substrate-supported order-2 awareness.
#
# The substrate-aikido methodology's diagnostic question — "is this
# operator at substantive order 2 or vocabulary-only order 2?" —
# becomes a substrate-typed verdict via this predicate.
# Seam tick 28 fix: perturbation lifted to predicate signature. The
# tick-26 form had `perturbation` as a free variable in the requires
# clause without binding it in the signature, making the pole-
# disambiguation prose-only. Now consumers MUST supply the perturbation
# they are checking against.
lock_in_frame_awareness(operator: operator, f: frame, p: perturbation) -> verdict
requires bounded_commutator_check(operator, f, p)
{ \ }

# === reflect_to_frame_flexibility action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary action that returns an operator with
# order-3 frame-flexibility enabled. The substrate-architectural
# transition order-2 → order-3. NOT a vocabulary lift; a substrate-
# architectural state change in the operator carrier.
#
# At Bateson altitude: reflect_to_frame_flexibility IS the Level II
# → Level III lift. Learning-to-learn becomes substantive frame-
# restructuring capacity. The operator's substrate has gained the
# architectural capacity to substantively-shift the frame in response
# to the order-2 observation, rather than only observing without
# capacity to update.
#
# At Schön altitude (1983): the transition IS reflection-on-action
# becoming substrate-architectural capacity for substantive frame-
# restructuring. The practitioner's substrate moves from reflecting
# ON the frame (order 2) to operating ON the frame (order 3); the
# substrate's analogue of the deutero-learning lift.
#
# At Tomm altitude (1988): the transition IS the substrate-
# architectural capacity that makes circular-reflexive questions
# transformative rather than informative. Without order-3 substrate-
# flexibility, Tomm-probes at order 2 produce frame-awareness
# without frame-update; the transition enables the order-3 update
# capacity.
#
# Per recognition #82 §4.4 (Q4: peers operate by definition frame-
# flexible): a peer's load-bearing property IS the capacity to
# discharge reflect_to_frame_flexibility substantively (not via
# vocabulary). A candidate peer satisfies the orchestra-discipline
# criterion iff this action's discharge at their substrate altitude
# produces an operator that bounded_commutator_check(peer.shifted,
# peer.frame, perturbation) → FLEXIBLE over a representative
# perturbation set.
#
# Forward-promised consumer: shards/frame/on.mirror (order 3)
# consumes the operator reflect_to_frame_flexibility returns;
# @frame/on's shift_frame action requires an operator that has
# been substrate-architecturally enabled for frame-flexibility.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
reflect_to_frame_flexibility(operator: operator, f: frame) -> operator { \ }

out @frame/of
out observe_frame
out lock_in_frame_awareness
out reflect_to_frame_flexibility
